According to a new report from Intel Market Research, the global AI Care Companion Robot market was valued at USD 30.12 million in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 185.67 million by 2034, growing at a robust CAGR of 34.2% during the forecast period (2025 2034). This expansion is driven by accelerating adoption of assistive robotics, expanding senior care budgets, and rapid advances in artificial intelligence integration that enhance safety critical functions such as fall detection and real time health monitoring.
AI care companion robots are specialized robotic systems designed to provide companionship, assistance, and support to individuals, particularly seniors or people with disabilities. These devices integrate artificial intelligence capabilities such as natural language processing, computer vision analytics, and adaptive learning algorithms, enabling functions that range from medication reminders and activity monitoring to conversational engagement and emergency alerts.
